WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.156 --> 00:00:15.717
During August, Pollyanna often visited Mr.

2
00:00:15.757 --> 00:00:18.699
Pendleton, but she wasn't sure how much her visits helped him.

3
00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:26.245
"He seems to like to hear me talk," she thought one afternoon as she walked home through Pendleton

4
00:00:26.265 --> 00:00:28.026
Woods. She smiled.

5
00:00:28.046 --> 00:00:30.728
"And I do like to talk!"

6
00:00:32.792 --> 00:00:35.433
But she had trouble predicting which topics would upset him.

7
00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:41.036
Today she had tried to tell him about the Glad Game, but he cut her off when she

8
00:00:41.096 --> 00:00:41.956
mentioned her father.

9
00:00:44.497 --> 00:00:46.918
Pollyanna remembered Nancy's idea that Mr.

10
00:00:46.978 --> 00:00:49.159
Pendleton and Aunt Polly had been engaged.

11
00:00:49.179 --> 00:00:53.621
"I'm beginning to think Nancy was right.

12
00:00:54.942 --> 00:01:00.164
Sometimes he's interested in what I say about Aunt Polly; other times he gets irritable.

13
00:01:01.608 --> 00:01:05.470
But he always listens with a strange smile on his face."

14
00:01:08.191 --> 00:01:11.072
Pollyanna stopped to watch two squirrels chasing each other.

15
00:01:11.092 --> 00:01:15.954
"Oh, I wish I could bring Aunt Polly and Mr.

16
00:01:16.014 --> 00:01:17.054
Pendleton together!

17
00:01:17.074 --> 00:01:21.756
They're both so lonely, but I don't know how to help them.

18
00:01:23.317 --> 00:01:26.358
Aunt Polly never wants to hear what I have to say about him.

19
00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:29.980
Then again, she never wants to hear about Dr.

20
00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:30.680
Chilton either.

21
00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:35.566
But that's probably because he saw her dressed up with the rose and shawl."

22
00:01:39.388 --> 00:01:43.210
Later that week Pollyanna again noticed Aunt Polly's dislike of Dr.

23
00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:47.692
Chilton. Pollyanna was in bed with a bad cold.

24
00:01:47.712 --> 00:01:53.075
"If you aren't better by tonight, I'm sending for the doctor," Aunt Polly said.

25
00:01:53.095 --> 00:01:56.017
"Then I hope I get worse."

26
00:01:57.178 --> 00:01:58.258
Pollyanna giggled.

27
00:01:58.278 --> 00:02:00.599
"I'd love to have Dr.

28
00:02:00.659 --> 00:02:01.520
Chilton visit."

29
00:02:03.284 --> 00:02:07.446
"Dr. Chilton is not our family physician," Aunt Polly said firmly.

30
00:02:07.466 --> 00:02:09.247
"I'll ask Dr.

31
00:02:09.287 --> 00:02:10.167
Warren to come."

32
00:02:10.187 --> 00:02:12.728
"I like Dr.

33
00:02:12.768 --> 00:02:14.469
Warren, but I like Dr.

34
00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:15.269
Chilton better.

35
00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:16.910
And Dr.

36
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.051
Chilton would feel hurt if I didn't use him.

37
00:02:20.192 --> 00:02:22.853
It wasn't his fault that he saw you looking so pretty."

38
00:02:22.873 --> 00:02:26.394
"That will do, Pollyanna.

39
00:02:26.414 --> 00:02:28.355
I do not wish to discuss Dr.

40
00:02:28.395 --> 00:02:30.036
Chilton or his feelings."

41
00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.561
Pollyanna studied her aunt's face.

42
00:02:33.581 --> 00:02:37.583
"I'd love to fix your hair again, Aunt Polly.

43
00:02:37.844 --> 00:02:41.726
Wait—" But Aunt Polly had already left Pollyanna's room.

44
00:02:43.787 --> 00:02:46.008
That evening there was no need to summon a doctor.

45
00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.952
After Pollyanna had recovered, she paid another visit to Mr.

46
00:02:51.972 --> 00:02:58.956
Pendleton. Upon entering his room, she cried, "There's a rainbow on your pillow!

47
00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:04.001
How did it get inside the house?"

48
00:03:04.021 --> 00:03:07.443
"Do you see that thermometer hanging outside the window?"

49
00:03:08.804 --> 00:03:10.044
Mr. Pendleton pointed.

50
00:03:10.064 --> 00:03:15.087
"Sunlight striking its glass edge causes a prism effect."

51
00:03:15.107 --> 00:03:19.029
"Oh, that's so beautiful!

52
00:03:19.609 --> 00:03:21.851
I wish I could live in a rainbow."

53
00:03:24.252 --> 00:03:28.294
Mr. Pendleton laughed as he watched Pollyanna happily studying the colors.

54
00:03:28.314 --> 00:03:31.356
"Let's see what we can do about that."

55
00:03:33.024 --> 00:03:35.926
He touched a bell beside his bed, and the maid soon appeared.

56
00:03:35.946 --> 00:03:39.588
"Bring me a brass candlestick from the drawing room mantel."

57
00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.371
As the maid returned, Pollyanna heard tinkling.

58
00:03:47.872 --> 00:03:52.815
She noticed glass pendants hanging from the candlestick.

59
00:03:52.835 --> 00:03:56.477
"Oh, those pendants are making such a pretty musical sound!"

60
00:03:58.057 --> 00:04:02.380
Mr. Pendleton asked the maid to remove a curtain and stretch a string across the window.

61
00:04:06.198 --> 00:04:08.660
Then he slipped a dozen pendants from the candlestick.

62
00:04:10.641 --> 00:04:16.365
"Now, Pollyanna, hook these glass pieces onto the string.

63
00:04:17.506 --> 00:04:20.668
If you really want to live in a rainbow, we'll make one for you."

64
00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.692
Pollyanna hung three pendants in the sunlit window.

65
00:04:28.273 --> 00:04:32.476
She was so excited that her hands trembled and she could barely finish the job.

66
00:04:35.068 --> 00:04:37.630
At last she stepped back to admire her work.

67
00:04:39.631 --> 00:04:42.993
"It's like a fairyland!"

68
00:04:43.353 --> 00:04:43.873
she cried.

69
00:04:45.094 --> 00:04:48.256
The entire room was aglow with shimmering bits of color.

70
00:04:48.276 --> 00:04:51.938
"Perhaps the sun is trying to play the game!

71
00:04:53.999 --> 00:04:56.761
Oh, I wish I had prisms to give to Mrs.

72
00:04:56.861 --> 00:04:58.562
Snow and lots of folks.

73
00:04:59.963 --> 00:05:01.564
Nancy's birthday is next week.

74
00:05:02.528 --> 00:05:05.510
And they'd make Aunt Polly so glad, she'd bang doors."

75
00:05:09.453 --> 00:05:10.634
Mr. Pendleton laughed.

76
00:05:10.654 --> 00:05:14.196
"It would take more than prisms to make your aunt do that.

77
00:05:15.497 --> 00:05:16.878
But what is this game you mentioned?"

78
00:05:18.339 --> 00:05:22.101
Pollyanna explained the game and told him the story of the doll and crutches.

79
00:05:23.902 --> 00:05:26.104
This time he didn't mind hearing about her father.

80
00:05:27.185 --> 00:05:28.445
Tears came to his eyes.

81
00:05:28.465 --> 00:05:32.880
"I think you're the finest prism of all," he said.

82
00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:37.324
"No, beautiful colors don't shine through me.

83
00:05:38.385 --> 00:05:39.826
The sun just gives me freckles."

84
00:05:43.149 --> 00:05:46.772
Mr. Pendleton laughed, but Pollyanna thought it sounded more like a sob.

85
00:05:48.333 --> 00:05:50.135
He pressed the bell to summon the maid again.

86
00:05:50.155 --> 00:05:54.738
"Pollyanna, I'm sending you home with prisms for you and your friends.

87
00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.221
And a gold coin for Nancy's birthday."

88
00:05:58.241 --> 00:06:01.084
"Oh, thank you, sir!"
